    "input_selector_source": "OwlDonationDone passes its event context +0x2a8 to F780E0; DA3FC0 uses its first byte, replacing values >7 with 0xff.",
    "query_behavior": "EF62F0 queries mode 2. EAA8C0 returns 0xffffffff if the current state token mismatches or the selected state view is absent/errored; otherwise it returns the byte at that view +0xb0d. F780E0 forwards the returned low byte into F78130.",
    "state_byte_producer": {
      "producer_va": "0xe68280",
      "lookup_va": "0xe68900",
      "state_record_stride": "0xb28",
      "state_record_slots": 8,
      "successful_query_condition": "EAA8C0 verifies the mode-2 context token, resolves a row index through EAA990/E68900, then returns 0xffffffff unless the row is active and +0xb08 is 0; on success it returns row +0xb0d as u8.",
      "writes": [
        "E68280 initializes the selected row as kind 3/inactive with u16 +0xb0d = 0x0100; for param_2 < 3 it writes the state kind at +0xb08, active byte +0xb0c = 1, param_3 to byte +0xb0d, and param_4 & 1 at +0xb0e.",
        "E68280's row is selected from eight 0xb28-byte records; E68900 checks the requested index is below eight and the row active byte at +0xb0c is nonzero."
      ],
      "direct_callers": [
        {
          "va": "0xccd40",
          "observed_arguments": "two branches call E68280(row, 2, 0, 1); active kind-2 rows are rejected by EAA8C0 mode 2"
        },
        {
          "va": "0xcd9f0",
          "observed_arguments": "FA4300 maps an identity pair to an existing slot 0..7; on match, E68280(row, 0, slot, 1)"
        },
        {
          "va": "0x2ee460",
          "observed_arguments": "when FA3C10 finds no pair match, FA4100 allocates the pair in a free slot 0..7; after associated context copies, E68280(row, 0, slot, 1)"
        },
        {
          "va": "0x2f5240",
          "observed_arguments": "called by 0x2f4f40 with the 0x2f5030 result; 0x2f5030 selects a 0..7 slot whose MakeVillagePlayerFlag query succeeds, or returns 0xffffffff"
        },
        {
          "va": "0xe684f0",
          "observed_arguments": "wrapper called by 0xcfad0; forwards kind 0/1 and param_3 from a runtime configuration row"
        }
      ],
      "meaning_status": "Two kind-0 paths use 0..7 indices into an eight-entry identity-pair map, and another selects the MakeVillagePlayerFlag slot (the local EventFlow crosswalk calls this the island representative). The exact runtime keys in the E684F0/CFAD0 configuration remain unknown, and these callers do not prove that the Museum marker denotes the donor or a donation-status enum.",
      "evidence": "Static Ghidra decompilation of the original NSO plus bounded fixture output at museum_donation_followup/marker_state_native.json; caller objects and live save state were not executed."
